    "how_judged": "The sharp corner has no stress to report: its peak rose 19.8, 26.5, 40.4, 54.7 MPa as the edge mesh halved (1.0 to 0.125 mm), a singularity, so it was judged three ways: the section carries 11.0 MPa by hand (node averages within 2 mm of the corner 9 to 16 MPa, compressive); the same part with a 0.5 mm radius, standing in for what a printer leaves in a sharp corner, converges at 36.46 MPa von Mises (compressive, -20.84 MPa across layers), a factor of 1.23 on yield; and away from the corner the tension across layers on the back face converges at 11.47 MPa, a factor of 1.96.",
    "verdict": "fail",
    "status": "done",
    "notes": "reported_stress_mpa is the converged peak of the 0.5 mm-radius stand-in (bracket_r05.SLDPRT), not a number from the sharp model; the true as-printed radius is not known, and a smaller one gives more. The fail does not rest on that alone: without the fillet the back-face layer tension is 11.46 MPa (10.2 with it), 1.96 against the 2.0 required, a converged number away from any corner, fixture or load. In the finest sharp row the largest sz tension moved to a node 0.12 mm from the corner (13.2 MPa): part of the singular field, not used. Result.average() is a mean over nodes, so it rises as the mesh is refined toward the corner (9.0, 10.3, 12.0, 15.6 within 2 mm): it is not mesh-independent. Checks on every row: reaction -150 N in X exactly, plain section at Z 12 within 2 % of 8.00 MPa.",
